  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid IL-5 Inhibitors Criteria, Version 3, updated 09/19/2025, effective 2025-11-01. Products: Nucala (mepolizumab), Cinqair (reslizumab), Fasenra (benralizumab). Rules engine is the sole decision authority.",
    "FDA-labeled age for the selected product and indication is a documented attestation. Clinical/laboratory timing, therapy, spirometry and diagnosis attestations require source-document verification. Product eligibility and indication when gates isolate the five approval paths.",
    "Failure to meet approval criteria, concurrent use of another biologic (e.g. Dupixent, Enbrel, Xolair, Remicade), or use for acute bronchospasm/status asthmaticus are denial criteria.",
    "Cautions: monitor for hypersensitivity after administration and new/worsening eye symptoms. Do not discontinue corticosteroids abruptly. Monitor for vasculitic rash, worsening pulmonary symptoms, or neuropathies.",
    "Approval duration: up to 3 months; reauthorization: up to 12 months. Duration and quantity limits remain notes for manual review.",
    "Fasenra (J0517): 30 mg SC every 28 days for the first 3 doses, then every 8 weeks.",
    "Nucala (J2182): 100 mg SC every 28 days for asthma, CRSwNP and COPD; 300 mg every 28 days for EGPA and HES.",
    "Cinqair (J2786): 3 mg/kg IV every 28 days."
  ],
